{
  "$comment": "Every surface a branding update must reach. brand/AGENTS.md has the rule; node brand/tools/audit.mjs checks each one. Paths in header, image, icon and og are relative to brand/ and must be in brand/provenance.json.",
  "version": 1,
  "canonicalRaw": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ourostack/.github/main/brand/",
  "org": "ourostack",
  "excluded": {
    "playwright": "Fork of microsoft/playwright. Its main mirrors upstream exactly as the base for upstream PR branches, so it keeps upstream's README; its About line (labs) says why we fork it.",
    "swift-toolkit": "Fork of readium/swift-toolkit, the reader engine Gatefold uses. Its default branch (develop) mirrors upstream exactly as the base for the branches where we prepare Gatefold's reader fixes to send upstream, so it keeps upstream's README; its About line (labs) says why we fork it.",
    "hyperellipse": "Fork of mikhailmogilnikov/hyperellipse, the corner-shape polyfill Ouro UI's squircles use where a browser has no native corner-shape (ourostack/ouro-ui-core docs/decisions/2026-11-13-squircles-switch-avatars.md). Its main mirrors upstream exactly until we need to tweak it, so it keeps upstream's README; its About line (labs) says why we fork it.",
    "image-gen-mcp": "Archived.",
    "npm:ouro.bot": "The ouro.bot npm wrapper ships no README; its page says so. If it ever ships one, add it here."
  },
  "outOfScope": "App icons (Ouro MD's icon, the Apple apps' icons) are product identity, not brand surfaces; they are not changed by a brand update. GitHub organization avatar is the approved rich Ouro render (2026-10-14); the Ouro Labs enterprise shows the same render and is registered below as enterprise:avatar so the audit notices if they drift apart.",
